    "AI Notes": {
      "value": "Alec Soth (b. 1969, Minneapolis) is one of the most prominent American art photographers of his generation, a full Magnum member since 2008 (nominee 2004). Work centers on large-format, on-the-road portraiture of the American Midwest; books include Sleeping by the Mississippi (2004), Niagara (2006), Broken Manual (2010), Songbook (2015), I Know How Furiously Your Heart Is Beating (2019), A Pound of Pictures (2022), and Advice for Young Artists (MACK, 2024). Gallery representation: Sean Kelly (New York), Fraenkel Gallery (San Francisco), Weinstein Hammons (Minneapolis), Loock Galerie (Berlin). Awards include the 2003 Santa Fe Prize, a 2013 Guggenheim Fellowship, and a 2021 Honorary Fellowship of the Royal Photographic Society. Runs Little Brown Mushroom, an independent publishing and multimedia venture (founded 2008/2010). Autonomy 5 (fully independent author-photographer, sets all creative direction, self-publishes, no employer): well above confidence floor.",
      "source_url": "https://alecsoth.com/photography/",
      "verified_at": "2026-07-01T01:21:11",
